// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'schemaId'. Valid alternatives: ['id', 'location', 'content']
//
// `schemaId` is a BINDING keyword. Inside a SchemaSet's `schemas:` entry the field is `id`.
// Two spellings for the same referent, one legal on each side of the reference, and the
// diagnostic here lists exactly what a schema entry accepts.
//
// Paired with neg-extformat-id-on-binding.pure, its exact mirror. A rewritten parser that
// gives SchemaSet and Binding one shared "identifier field" rule accepts both files and
// produces a SchemaSet whose id legend-engine would have refused to read.
###ExternalFormat
SchemaSet fixture::neg::SchemaIdOnSchemaSet
{
   format: FlatData;
   schemas: [
      {
         schemaId: primary;
         location: 'people.schema';
         content: 'section people: DelimitedWithHeadings\n{\n  scope.untilEof;\n  delimiter: \',\';\n\n  Record\n  {\n    NAME : STRING;\n  }\n}';
      }
   ];
}
